abstract: >-
  eskaks is a high-performance command-line tool for calculating pairwise dN/dS
  (Ka/Ks) ratios from codon-aligned sequences. It implements the Nei-Gojobori
  (1986) and Li (1993) / Pamilo-Bianchi (1993) models with precomputed lookup
  tables, achieving over 1,000× speedup compared to existing tools while
  maintaining numerical accuracy (R² = 1.0 vs KaKs_Calculator for the Li model).
  Supports 20 NCBI genetic code tables, parallel computation, sliding window
  analysis, and multiple output formats (TSV, CSV, JSON).
